# The corpus fixtures are byte-exact contracts: the importer regenerates
# converted-markdown and the anchor tests regenerate heading-anchors, and CI
# fails if the committed bytes differ from what the code produces. CRLF
# smudging via core.autocrlf breaks that equality (and made the round-trip
# tests fail in a fresh autocrlf=true clone), so pin them to LF everywhere.
tests/fixtures/** text eol=lf

# Same byte-exactness argument: the schema-drift test compares this file to
# the exporter's output.
schema.graphql text eol=lf
